In this problem, we can use the logarithm property of exponentiation to solve it. We can check whether the given number is a power of three by finding its base-3 logarithm and checking if the result is an integer. If it is, then the number is a power of three; otherwise, it is not.

Here is the implementation in Java:
```java
public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n < 1) {
        return false;
    }
    double log3 = Math.log(n) / Math.log(3);
    return (log3 == (int) log3);
}
```
This solution has a time complexity of O(log n), which is optimal as it requires calculating the base-3 logarithm.user

